**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG
**Related Spec**: specs/438-return-write-spec-to-native-plan-mode-after-merged-publication/

# File: scripts/__tests__/extension-commands.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/444-exit-native-plan-mode-when-write-spec-finished-is-selected/requirements.md
Feature: Exit native plan mode when write-spec Finished is selected
  Selecting Finished in either write-spec picker left the TUI session in
  native plan mode, so the write-spec cycle could not stop.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Continue-loop Finished exits plan mode fully
    Given a write-spec continuation running in native plan mode after issue 450 was published
    When the Continue picker returns "Finished — stop writing specs" and the turn ends terminally
    Then the extension dispatches builtin /plan twice through the focused TUI editor
    And the session mode is recorded as plan_paused and then none
    And the continuation prompt was submitted exactly once and no other command is dispatched

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Initial-picker Finished exits plan mode fully
    Given bare /sdlc-write-spec running in native plan mode
    When the initial picker returns "Finished — stop without writing a spec" and the turn ends terminally
    Then the extension dispatches builtin /plan twice through the focused TUI editor
    And the last session mode is none and no notification is shown

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Non-Finished selections keep plan mode
    Given a write-spec session in native plan mode
    When a picker returns "#445 — Next issue", "Continue — enter another issue number", custom input "#12", or custom input "abc" and the turn ends terminally
    Then no /plan command is dispatched
    And the session mode stays plan

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Undispatchable exit fails safe
    Given "Finished — stop writing specs" was selected in a write-spec session in native plan mode
    When the terminal turn ends with no UI, the editor draft "my draft", an unfocused editor, a throwing submit, or a declined exit confirmation
    Then the editor draft is unchanged and no partial command is submitted
    And the warning "NMG SDLC: write-spec finished, but plan mode is still active; /plan exits it." is shown once
    And a later terminal turn end dispatches nothing
    And a non-terminal turn end before the terminal one dispatches nothing

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Post-publication continuation is preserved
    Given merged write-spec publications for issues 400 and 402 in one TUI process
    When each execution turn ends terminally
    Then the Continue prompt is submitted into plan mode exactly once per publication listing every published N-slug
    And a new /sdlc-write-spec invocation resets the published list and a pending Finished exit
